properties.description:
Nine tests.

Router level, six in registry_http.rs, against real stores:
- a full router closes its least recently used design instead of refusing, and the closed one reopens;
- busy (503, Retry-After 5) only while every open design has a request in flight;
- a design is not reopened until its previous copy lets go of the store;
- an idle design is closed and a busy one is not;
- no idle timeout closes nothing;
- an unknown id is 404 and takes no place.

Over the real binary and HTTP, three in a_server_closes_designs_nobody_is_using.rs:
- three designs behind a limit of two all answer; a write survives the close; the old session is 404; re-initializing works;
- the idle sweep closes a design with no request to prompt it;
- an unknown id is still 404.

Two guards were observed failing under mutation: removing the release wait (RocksDB: "lock hold by current process"), and replacing LRU with refusal.
